chor":"Structures"},{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init()","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(_:)-2unw2","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(_:)-6cbnw","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(adjacency:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(edges:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(vertices:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(vertices:edges:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/insert(edge:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/CustomDebugStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/CustomReflectable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Decodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Encodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteral-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Hashable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/MutableDirectedGraph-Implementations"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdjacencyList"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertex set is any set of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values. The edge set is a set of ordered pairs of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot. Edges are kept in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, so an edge’s position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":", and a weight can live"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in an array beside the graph. Each slot has a row of the slots of its out-neighbors, a parallel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row of those edges’ positions, and a row of its in-neighbors; the rows of each kind share one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however many vertices it has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(amortized, like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":"), and copying it copies a constant number of buffers. A dictionary from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slot pair to position answers "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in O(1)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each row"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule"]]},"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate: Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" concept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_vertex"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_edge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_edge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_vertex"},{"type":"text","text":"), for a directed representation. It exists so that a wrapper which adds a rule, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can own any of the mutable representations as its base and still run at the base’s speed."}],"title":"MutableDirectedGraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertices","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P8VerticesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://AdjacencyListModule/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://AdjacencyListModule/documentation/AdjacencyListModule/AdjacencyList/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations":{"role":"collectionGroup","title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/adjacencylistmodule\/adjacencylist\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph-implementations","abstract":[],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","type":"topic"},"doc://AdjacencyListModule/documentation/AdjacencyListModule/AdjacencyList/Decodable-Implementations":{"role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[],"title":"Decodabl